},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every record in the section LinkerSets owns starts with a kind, and enumeration returns only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the records of the kind asked for, so many clients share one section without seeing each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other’s records. A kind is a 32-bit value, conventionally four ASCII characters read as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"big-endian integer, as Swift Testing’s test-content kinds are (","type":"text"},{"code":"0x74657374","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"test\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["extension LinkerSetKind {","    \/\/\/ Records of routes, `\"rout\"`.","    static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A client picks one kind for its records and keeps it: records already compiled into other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"modules carry the value they were built with. Kind 0 is reserved: it marks a slot that holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no record, and a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSet"},{"type":"text","text":" of it is always empty."}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/linkersetkind"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetKind","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/s15BitwiseCopyableP","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/SQ","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/SH","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/SY","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"references"